<title>USA: Richmond Fed - Feb manufacturing, services indexes.</title>
<headline>Richmond Fed - Feb manufacturing, services indexes.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond indexes monitoring manufacturing and service-sector activity in January.</p>
<p> MANUFACTURING SURVEY     Feb    Jan</p>
<p>  Shipments		   -10     -9</p>
<p>  New Orders		   -1	3</p>
<p>  Backlog Orders	    -15	0</p>
<p>  Number of Employees	-5     -7</p>
<p>  Average Workweek	   -3     -6</p>
<p>  Prices Received	 -0.14   0.07</p>
<p>  Prices Paid		0.31   0.53</p>
<p> SERVICES SURVEY	    Feb    Jan</p>
<p>  Service Revenues	    8     12</p>
<p>  Number of Employees	 4	1</p>
<p>  Service Wage		 14     24</p>
<p>  Retail Revenues	     9	0</p>
<p>  Retail Employees	  -10    -12</p>
<p>  Retail Wage		   7     12</p>
<p>  Shopper Traffic	     3	0</p>
<p>Indicators of manufacturing growth changed little on balance in February, the Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond said in its survey.</p>
<p>It said respondents indicated that they expected finished goods and raw materials prices to rise at a somewhat slower pace over the next six months. Service producers and retailers expected smaller price increases for the next six months.</p>
